# Frontend Development Rules

- React 19.3 automatic JSX runtime, Vite 8. No router, no state library, no component library, no CSS framework.
- State is local `useState` / `useRef` only. `src/main.tsx` owns the app shell and cross-panel state.
- One plain stylesheet `src/style.css` with BEM-ish class names.
- All HTTP goes through `api<T>()` in `src/api.ts`. Never call `fetch` directly.
- Preserve the `alive` unmount guard and the sequence-number async guard. Autosave stays debounced (400 ms) and serialized.
- Display money only via `money()`, durations only via `formatDuration()`. `money(null)` renders `Unknown`.
- Accessibility is load-bearing: `tests/*.spec.ts` selects only by role and accessible name. Errors use `role="alert"`, status uses `role="status"`. No overflow at 390px.
- Named exports only, inline prop types, one component per file.
